  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "typepick",
      "page": "typeface",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -270,
      "w": 960,
      "text": "Settled: ATKINSON HYPERLEGIBLE.\n\nKept as the record of what was compared. All four were self-hosted candidates; three were SIL OFL 1.1, which is the practical ceiling for a usable UI face - so the licence never separated them, and provenance and character did.\n\nWorth remembering from this page: DejaVu, the one picked for licence freedom, had the least clear paperwork of the four. And IBM Plex is IBM's, not Google's - Google Fonts only mirrors it."
    },
    {
      "id": "gate",
      "page": "foundations",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -250,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "APPROVED: PETROL + CONSOLE + ATKINSON HYPERLEGIBLE. This is the binding handoff for tokens.css.\n\nThe form study's one conflict is resolved here: display rows sit at 40 px, but any row holding a control is 52 px so the control keeps its full 44 px target.\n\nThe typeface is vendored, not fetched: two subset variable woff2, 30.3 and 15.4 KB, covering weights 200-800 of both families. No font host, no CDN, works offline.\n\nEvery contrast number is computed by tools/palette-report.mjs. All 27 pairs pass in both appearances."
    },
    {
      "id": "formpick",
      "page": "form",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Settled: CONSOLE.\n\nKept as the record of what was compared. All three dropped the card-in-a-card habit; Console won because the row - not the box - became the unit."
    },
    {
      "id": "pick",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Settled: PETROL.\n\nKept as the record. Each candidate changed hue, chroma, form and type together, and all 27 contrast pairs pass in both appearances for every one of them - so the choice was about character, not about which one was safe."
    }
  ],
